import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.C1oW5ckO.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Publishing public npm tools","description":"Placeholder setup and Release Please publishing for public npm tools","frontmatter":{"navigation":{"category":"CI and releases"},"title":"Publishing public npm tools","description":"Placeholder setup and Release Please publishing for public npm tools","editLink":"https://github.com/filiphsps/pumpkin-plugins/edit/master/docs/npm-publishing.md"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"guides/npm-publishing.md","filePath":"docs/npm-publishing.md","lastUpdated":1792080313000}`),a={name:`guides/npm-publishing.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="publishing-public-npm-tools" tabindex="-1">Publishing public npm tools <a class="header-anchor" href="#publishing-public-npm-tools" aria-label="Permalink to “Publishing public npm tools”">​</a></h1><p>Public npm tools are discovered from package manifests under <code>tools/</code> that declare <code>publishConfig.access: &quot;public&quot;</code> and are not private. Their package manifests and packed project templates declare the dependencies that determine release order.</p><p>For initial setup, publish metadata-only placeholders at <code>0.0.0</code>. Release Please produces and the GitHub Actions release workflow publishes the first functional release for each package.</p><h2 id="seed-package-names" tabindex="-1">Seed package names <a class="header-anchor" href="#seed-package-names" aria-label="Permalink to “Seed package names”">​</a></h2><p>npm requires a package to exist before a trusted publisher can be configured. Publish one <code>0.0.0</code> placeholder for each public tool before setting up trusted publishing. Each placeholder contains only <code>package.json</code> and a README that says the package is non-functional. It must not contain runtime code, commands, or package dependencies.</p><p>Publish each verified placeholder tarball with the <code>placeholder</code> dist-tag:</p><div class="language-sh"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark" style="--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">npm</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> publish</span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> &lt;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">placeholder-tarbal</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">l</span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">&gt;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --access</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> public</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --tag=placeholder</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The registry also assigns the first published version to <code>latest</code>, so both tags point to <code>0.0.0</code> until the first functional release. The release workflow publishes without a non-default tag, moving <code>latest</code> to the functional version while <code>placeholder</code> remains on <code>0.0.0</code>.</p><p>Run direct npm commands from outside the repository root, such as <code>/tmp</code>, to avoid the root <code>devEngines</code> package-manager requirement. Confirm the exact package name and <code>0.0.0</code> version on the public registry after each publish. Do not republish a placeholder version with different bytes; npm versions are immutable.</p><h2 id="publish-functional-releases" tabindex="-1">Publish functional releases <a class="header-anchor" href="#publish-functional-releases" aria-label="Permalink to “Publish functional releases”">​</a></h2><p>Release Please creates a tool&#39;s release PR only after its transitive public production dependencies have functional releases. The configured first functional version is <code>0.1.0</code>. The publish job orders selected tools from their declared production dependencies and packed project templates, so each consumer&#39;s required public dependencies are available before its publish job runs.</p><p>Release PR titles use the full <code>@pumpkin-plugins/&lt;name&gt;</code> package name for scoped tools, while tags keep using the folder component. The unscoped <code>create-pumpkin-plugin</code> title stays unscoped.</p><p>The <code>ci.yml</code> caller invokes the reusable release workflow after CI gates pass. Its <code>publish-tools</code> job scans non-draft public-tool releases on the target commit&#39;s first-parent history on every normal run. It checks which historical versions are missing from npm, then packs and publishes them from their exact release commits, oldest first. It publishes the current commit&#39;s selected tools after catch-up, checking exact dependency versions and registry integrity before using npm trusted publishing and provenance. When an exact-version prerequisite is not yet visible in npm, the publisher retries its lookup for up to about two minutes to allow registry propagation. This recovers releases when a rapid series of pushes replaces an older pending CI run. See <a href="/pumpkin-plugins/guides/npm-trusted-publishing">Trusted publishing for npm tools</a> for setup and recovery.</p><p>To recover immediately without another push, dispatch the <code>ci.yml</code> caller with the full commit SHA that the release tag targets. For codemod, resolve its tag before dispatching:</p><div class="language-sh"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark" style="--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">release_commit</span><span style="--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;$(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">git</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> rev-parse &#39;codemod-v0.1.0^{commit}&#39;)&quot;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">gh</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> workflow</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> run</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> ci.yml</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> --ref</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> master</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> -f</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> release_commit=&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">$release_commit</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;</span></span></code></pre></div><p>This recovery reads existing GitHub releases without creating release tags or PRs, selects only npm tools whose tags point to that exact SHA, then checks out the same source commit for packing. Normal push releases remain pinned to the commit built by their own workflow run. Replace the tag with the target tool&#39;s release tag when recovering another package.</p><p>Configure trust for a package only after its placeholder exists and its real Release Please release is ready. The first successful OIDC publish must complete within two days of creating the relationship. Publishing the existing <code>0.0.0</code> placeholder again does not validate OIDC.</p><p><code>pnpm npm:bootstrap</code> is available as a manual exact-tag fallback for a maintainer who must publish a <code>0.1.0</code> artifact directly. It validates the tagged source and package but does not configure npm trust. The normal first functional release uses the Release Please workflow above.</p>`,18)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};